  <content>
    <description>
      <levelledPara>
        <title>General</title>
        <para>
          The Central Warning System (CWS) provides crew alerting through a structured message model
          supporting multiple priority levels. This data module describes the message taxonomy,
          prioritization logic, and display characteristics for CAS/ECAM/EICAS systems.
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Message Priority Levels</title>
        <para>
          The system supports five distinct alert priority levels:
        </para>
        <para>
          <randomList>
            <listItem>
              <para>
                <emphasis emphasisType="em02">Level 1 - Warning (RED):</emphasis>
                Requires immediate crew action. Indicates a potentially catastrophic condition.
                Accompanied by continuous tone or voice aural alert and master warning light.
              </para>
            </listItem>
            <listItem>
              <para>
                <emphasis emphasisType="em02">Level 2 - Caution (AMBER):</emphasis>
                Requires timely crew awareness and action. Indicates abnormal condition that could
                become hazardous. Accompanied by single chime and master caution light.
              </para>
            </listItem>
            <listItem>
              <para>
                <emphasis emphasisType="em02">Level 3 - Advisory (WHITE/CYAN):</emphasis>
                Crew awareness required for non-normal system configuration. No immediate action
                required. No aural alert.
              </para>
            </listItem>
            <listItem>
              <para>
                <emphasis emphasisType="em02">Level 4 - Status (WHITE/GREEN):</emphasis>
                Informational messages about normal system status. No crew action required.
              </para>
            </listItem>
            <listItem>
              <para>
                <emphasis emphasisType="em02">Level 5 - Memo (WHITE):</emphasis>
                Procedural reminders and configuration information. No aural alert.
              </para>
            </listItem>
          </randomList>
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Message Data Model</title>
        <para>
          Each alert message in the database contains the following elements:
        </para>
        <para>
          <randomList>
            <listItem><para>Unique Message Identifier (numeric ID)</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>Message Text (crew-facing description)</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>Priority Level (1-5)</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>Display Color (RGB specification)</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>Aural Alert Type (voice, tone, chime, none)</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>System Source (ATA chapter reference)</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>Triggering Condition(s)</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>Inhibit Logic Rules</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>Associated Crew Actions (if applicable)</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>Checklist References</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>BITE Data and Fault Codes</para></listItem>
          </randomList>
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Prioritization and Display Logic</title>
        <para>
          When multiple alerts are simultaneously active, the system applies the following rules:
        </para>
        <para>
          <randomList>
            <listItem><para>The highest priority alert is displayed prominently at the top of the alert list</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>Lower priority alerts may be suppressed or collapsed based on available display area</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>Alert lists are dynamically reordered as conditions change</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>Master warning/caution light state reflects highest active alert level</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>Only the highest priority aural alert is sounded (no stacking of aural alerts)</para></listItem>
          </randomList>
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
      
      <levelledPara>
        <title>Alert Inhibit Logic</title>
        <para>
          Certain alerts are inhibited during critical flight phases to reduce crew workload.
          Inhibit conditions are coordinated with the autoflight system (ATA 22) and include:
        </para>
        <para>
          <randomList>
            <listItem><para>Takeoff phase (thrust application to 1500' AGL)</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>Landing phase (below 200' AGL to touchdown)</para></listItem>
            <listItem><para>Go-around mode (initial climb-out)</para></listItem>
          </randomList>
        </para>
        <para>
          Critical warnings (engine fire, flight control failures) are never inhibited.
        </para>
      </levelledPara>
    </description>
